    "title": "Strict-endpoint residual-pole interpolation exclusion",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "pole-ideal interpolation and surface cohomology",
    "statement": "On every even m>=6 strict A=3, e=m endpoint profile, the pole-cancellation quotient for G(X)/H(z) has length at most O<=m-1. A nonzero biform of bidegree (1,m/2-1) therefore clears all poles without containing any component. Multiplying the resulting componentwise-nonzero grid section by four universal Forney contact sections gives a forbidden nonzero section of O_C(-7,m/2+2). Hence every e=m defect stratum is impossible, including the official m=2^37 row.",
